# Exalere Issue Labels Definition

This configuration lists standard labels to categorize issues, bugs, PRs, and roadmap cards on GitHub and GitHub Projects.

```json
[
  {
    "name": "bug",
    "color": "d73a4a",
    "description": "Something isn't working as expected"
  },
  {
    "name": "enhancement",
    "color": "a2eeef",
    "description": "New feature or request"
  },
  {
    "name": "tv-mode",
    "color": "0075ca",
    "description": "Android TV, Google TV, or remote D-Pad navigation related"
  },
  {
    "name": "player",
    "color": "7057ff",
    "description": "Video playback, media_kit, libmpv, or external player"
  },
  {
    "name": "windows",
    "color": "5319e7",
    "description": "Windows desktop platform specific"
  },
  {
    "name": "android",
    "color": "0e8a16",
    "description": "Android mobile or tablet specific"
  },
  {
    "name": "good first issue",
    "color": "7057ff",
    "description": "Good for newcomers to pick up"
  },
  {
    "name": "ai-contribution",
    "color": "fbca04",
    "description": "Contributions developed using AI coding agents"
  },
  {
    "name": "triage",
    "color": "ededed",
    "description": "Needs review or classification from maintainers"
  }
]
```
